.el .ds Aq '
.TH cadcraft-cli-mcp 1  "mcp " 
.SH NAME
cadcraft\-cli\-mcp \- Run the MCP server on stdio: a headless drawing session, or a bridge to the running app
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcadcraft\-cli mcp\fR [\fB\-\-connect\fR] [\fB\-\-lazy\fR] [\fB\-\-launch\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-fontalt\fR] [\fB\-\-fontfallback\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the MCP server on stdio: a headless drawing session, or a bridge to the running app
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-connect\fR \fI<HOST:PORT>\fR
Bridge to the app\*(Aqs control channel (its \-\-control port, e.g. 127.0.0.1:7979)
.TP
\fB\-\-lazy\fR
Reach the app at the first call instead of at startup, so the server can start before the app is open
.TP
\fB\-\-launch\fR
Like \-\-lazy, and a call that finds nothing at HOST:PORT opens the app with that control port first (macOS)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The settings folder; plotter configurations are in its `plotters` folder (default: the platform\*(Aqs settings folder). An empty value means no settings folder
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBCADCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fontalt\fR \fI<FONT>\fR
The font that replaces a missing one (FONTALT)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBCADCRAFT_FONTALT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fontfallback\fR \fI<FONTS>\fR
The fonts tried, in order, for characters a font lacks, comma\-separated (FONTFALLBACK)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBCADCRAFT_FONTFALLBACK\fR environment variable. 
.RE
